+## Rotate the Password
+
+To change the password without signing users out, pass a list instead of a single string. The first password seals new cookies, and the others only open existing ones:
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD],
+});
+```
+
+- Every password in the list must be at least 32 characters. An empty list, or a shorter password, makes reading the session throw an error.
+- A cookie opened with a password other than the first is resealed with the first one on the next read, so rotation moves forward without any action from the user. Only cookies are resealed. A session sent in the `x-{name}-session` header cannot be, so it keeps the old password until it expires.
+- Keep the old password until the longest session lifetime has passed: `maxAge`, or `idleTimeout` for sessions sent in the header. H3 cannot tell which sessions are still sealed with an old password, so removing it earlier signs out any session that still uses it.
+- Each extra password adds PBKDF2 work to reads that the passwords before it cannot open. A cookie that no password opens tries all of them. Keep the list short, three passwords at most.
+- Accepted old passwords widen the attack surface for as long as they stay in the list. Remove them as soon as the lifetime rule allows.
+
 ## Expiration
 
 Sessions have two independent expiration controls, and you can use either or both:
